<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 4 August, from 1265 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1265">1265 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">761 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simon de Montfort is killed at the Battle of Evesham</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The future Edward I defeated and killed Simon de Montfort at Evesham, ending the barons' rebellion against Henry III. Montfort's parliaments with elected burgesses outlived him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1320">1320 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">706 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Black Parliament tries plotters against Robert the Bruce</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A specially convened parliament at Scone tried William II de Soules, Lord of Liddesdale, and others who had conspired against King Robert I. Soules confessed his treason and was sentenced to life imprisonment; his fellow conspirators were executed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1356">1356 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">670 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward the Black Prince launches a large-scale mounted raid</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Anglo-Gascon force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a> began a large-scale chevauchée, or mounted raid, that lasted until 2 October. In the same year the prince captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1578">1578 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">448 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Moroccan forces destroy King Sebastian's army at Alcácer Quibir</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Ksar-el-Kebir, Moroccan forces destroyed the Portuguese army of King Sebastian, who was killed with much of the nobility. Sebastian's death without an heir led to the union of the Portuguese and Spanish crowns in 1580.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alcacer-quibir">Battle of Alcácer Quibir</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebastian-of-portugal">Sebastian of Portugal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1704">1704 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">322 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anglo-Dutch forces capture Gibraltar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A fleet under Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-rooke">Sir George Rooke</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. Ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1713, it remains a British territory despite repeated Spanish claims.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France's National Assembly abolishes feudal privileges</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a night session, nobles and clergy renounced their seigneurial rights, tithes and exemptions one after another. The decrees swept away much of the legal framework of the Ancien Régime.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1914">1914 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain declares war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> ignored an ultimatum to respect Belgian neutrality, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> declared war at 11 pm <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> time. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>'s entry turned a continental war into a global one.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne Frank and her family are arrested in Amsterdam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German police raided the secret annexe at Prinsengracht 263, arresting the Frank family and four others. Anne died in Bergen-Belsen in early 1945; her diary became a classic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> testimony.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1964">1964 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US destroyers report a second attack in the Gulf of Tonkin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US warships reported an attack by North Vietnamese boats that probably never happened. Within days Congress passed the Gulf of Tonkin Resolution, authorising Johnson to escalate the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
